@startuml Hybrid V2 Forward Pass Sequence

title Hybrid V2 Model - Forward Pass Sequence Diagram

actor Input as "Input Image\n(224×224×3)"
participant "ResNet50\nBackbone" as ResNet
participant "EfficientNet-B0\nBackbone" as EfficientNet
participant "Fusion\nModule" as Fusion
participant "Classifier" as Classifier
participant Output as "Output\nLogits"

== Feature Extraction (Parallel) ==

Input -> ResNet: Forward pass
activate ResNet
ResNet -> ResNet: Conv1 + BN + ReLU
ResNet -> ResNet: MaxPool
ResNet -> ResNet: Layer1 (3× Bottleneck)
ResNet -> ResNet: Layer2 (4× Bottleneck)
ResNet -> ResNet: Layer3 (6× Bottleneck)
ResNet -> ResNet: Layer4 (3× Bottleneck)
ResNet -> ResNet: Global Average Pooling
ResNet -> ResNet: Flatten
ResNet --> Fusion: ResNet Features (2048 dims)
deactivate ResNet

Input -> EfficientNet: Forward pass
activate EfficientNet
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: Stem Conv
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: MBConv Block 1
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: MBConv Block 2
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: MBConv Block 3
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: MBConv Block 4
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: MBConv Block 5
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: MBConv Block 6
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: MBConv Block 7
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: Global Average Pooling
EfficientNet -> EfficientNet: Flatten
EfficientNet --> Fusion: EfficientNet Features (1280 dims)
deactivate EfficientNet

== Feature Fusion ==

activate Fusion
Fusion -> Fusion: Concatenate([2048, 1280])
note right: Combined: 3328 dimensions
Fusion -> Fusion: Linear(3328 → 512)
Fusion -> Fusion: LayerNorm(512)
Fusion -> Fusion: ReLU()
Fusion -> Fusion: Dropout(0.3)
Fusion --> Classifier: Fused Features (512 dims)
deactivate Fusion

== Classification ==

activate Classifier
Classifier -> Classifier: Linear(512 → 12)
Classifier --> Output: Logits (12 classes)
deactivate Classifier

Output -> Output: Softmax (for inference)

note over ResNet, EfficientNet
  **Parallel Processing:**
  Both backbones process
  the same input image
  simultaneously
end note

note over Fusion
  **Fusion Strategy:**
  Combines complementary
  features from both models
  for enhanced representation
end note

@enduml


